=== fastp
--- fastp --in
--in1=	read1 input file name
--in2=	read2 input file name
--include_unmerged 	in the merging mode, write the unmerged or unpaired reads to the file specified by --merge
--interleaved_in 	indicate that <in1> is an interleaved FASTQ which contains both read1 and read2
--- fastp -i data/
data/ont.fastq 
data/r1.fq.gz 
data/r2.fq.gz 
data/sub/
--- fastp -i data/r1.fq.gz -o 
bio_reads.sh 
data/
--- fastp --adapter_fasta data/
data/adapters.fasta 
data/ref.fa 
data/sub/
--- fastp --umi_loc 
index1 
index2 
per_index 
per_read 
read1 
read2 
--- fastp -?
-? 	print this message
