data/ref.fa 
data/sub/
data/u.bam 
--- falco --stdin 
fq 
fq:4 
fq:6 
sam 
sam:4 
sam:6 
--- falco --no-
--no-adap 	toggle adapter analysis
--no-dups 	toggle sequence duplication analysis
--no-kmers 	toggle k-mer analysis
--no-tiles 	toggle per-tile quality analysis
=== cutadapt
--- cutadapt -a 
file:	adapters from a FASTA file
--- cutadapt -a file:data/
file:data/adapters.fasta 
file:data/ref.fa 
file:data/sub/
--- cutadapt -G ^file:data/
^file:data/adapters.fasta 
^file:data/ref.fa 
^file:data/sub/
--- cutadapt --action 
crop 
lowercase 
mask 
none 
retain 
trim 
--- cutadapt --pair-filter 
any 
both 
first 
--- cutadapt --discard
--discard 	discard reads that contain an adapter
--discard-casava 	discard reads that did not pass CASAVA filtering (header has :Y:)
--discard-trimmed 	discard reads that contain an adapter
--discard-untrimmed 	discard reads that do not contain an adapter
--- cutadapt -o out.fq data/
data/adapters.fasta 
data/ont.fastq 
data/r1.fq.gz 
data/r2.fq.gz 
data/ref.fa 
data/sub/
=== trimmomatic
--- trimmomatic 
PE 	paired-end reads: two inputs, four outputs, then steps
SE 	single-end reads: an input, an output, then steps
--- trimmomatic PE -
-basein 	the first input file, whose name gives the second's
-baseout 	the base name of the four output files
-phred33 	qualities are Phred+33
-phred64 	qualities are Phred+64
-quiet 	print only errors
-summary 	summary of the statistics
-threads 	number of threads
-trimlog 	log of the trimming of each read
-validatePairs 	check that the names of the pairs match
-version 	print the version
--- trimmomatic PE -phred33 data/
data/ont.fastq 
data/r1.fq.gz 
data/r2.fq.gz 
data/sub/
--- trimmomatic PE data/r1.fq.gz data/r2.fq.gz p1 u1 p2 u2 
AVGQUAL:	drop reads whose mean quality is below QUALITY
BASECOUNT:	drop reads by the count of some bases: BASES[:MIN[:MAX]]
CROP:	cut the read to a length: LENGTH
HEADCROP:	cut bases off the start: LENGTH
ILLUMINACLIP:	cut adapters: FASTA:MISMATCHES:PALINDROME:SIMPLE[:MINLEN:KEEPBOTH]
LEADING:	cut bases off the start below a quality: QUALITY
MAXINFO:	adaptive quality trimming: LENGTH:STRICTNESS
MAXLEN:	drop reads longer than LENGTH
MINLEN:	drop reads shorter than LENGTH
SLIDINGWINDOW:	cut once the mean quality of a window drops: SIZE:QUALITY
TAILCROP:	cut bases off the end: LENGTH
TOPHRED33 	convert the qualities to Phred+33
TOPHRED64 	convert the qualities to Phred+64
TRAILING:	cut bases off the end below a quality: QUALITY
bio_reads.sh 
data/
--- trimmomatic PE data/r1.fq.gz data/r2.fq.gz p1 u1 p2 u2 SL
SLIDINGWINDOW:	cut once the mean quality of a window drops: SIZE:QUALITY
--- trimmomatic SE data/r1.fq.gz out.fq ILLUMINACLIP:
ILLUMINACLIP:NexteraPE-PE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq2-PE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq2-SE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-PE-2-GGGGG.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-PE-2.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-PE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-SE-GGGGG.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-SE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:data/
--- trimmomatic SE data/r1.fq.gz out.fq ILLUMINACLIP:Tru
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq2-PE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq2-SE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-PE-2-GGGGG.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-PE-2.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-PE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-SE-GGGGG.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
ILLUMINACLIP:TruSeq3-SE.fa:	comes with Trimmomatic
--- trimmomatic SE data/r1.fq.gz out.fq ILLUMINACLIP:data/
ILLUMINACLIP:data/adapters.fasta:
ILLUMINACLIP:data/ref.fa:
ILLUMINACLIP:data/sub/
--- trimmomatic SE data/r1.fq.gz out.fq ILLUMINACLIP:data/adapters.fasta:2
--- trimmomatic PE -basein data/
data/ont.fastq 
data/r1.fq.gz 
data/r2.fq.gz 
data/sub/
=== trim_galore, fastq_screen
--- trim_galore --pa
--paired 	paired-end mode
--passthrough=	pass a third FASTQ file through unchanged but keep it in lockstep with R1/R2
--- trim_galore --output-format 
fastq 
ubam 
--- trim_galore -o data/
data/sub/
--- trim_galore --paired data/
data/ont.fastq 
data/r1.fq.gz 
data/r2.fq.gz 
data/sub/
--- fastq_screen --aligner 
bowtie 
bowtie2 
bwa 
minimap2 
--- fastq_screen --min
--minimap2=	specify extra parameters to be passed to minimap2
=== seqtk
--- seqtk 
comp 	get the nucleotide composition of FASTA/Q
cutN 	cut sequence at long N
dropse 	drop unpaired from interleaved PE FASTA/Q
famask 	apply a X-coded FASTA to a source FASTA
fqchk 	fastq QC (base/quality summary)
gap 	get the gap locations
gc 	identify high- or low-GC regions
hety 	regional heterozygosity
hpc 	homopolyer-compressed sequence
listhet 	extract the position of each het
mergefa 	merge two FASTA/Q files
mergepe 	interleave two PE FASTA/Q files
mutfa 	point mutate FASTA at specified positions
randbase 	choose a random base from hets
rename 	rename sequence names
sample 	subsample sequences
seq 	common transformation of FASTA/Q
size 	report the number sequences and bases
split 	split one file into multiple smaller files
subseq 	extract subsequences from FASTA/Q
telo 	identify telomere repeats in asm or long reads
trimfq 	trim FASTQ using the Phred algorithm
--- seqtk s
sample 	subsample sequences
seq 	common transformation of FASTA/Q
size 	report the number sequences and bases
split 	split one file into multiple smaller files
subseq 	extract subsequences from FASTA/Q
--- seqtk seq -
-1 	output the 2n-1 reads only
-2 	output the 2n reads only
-A 	force FASTA output (discard quality)
-C 	drop comments at the header lines
-F 	fake FASTQ quality
-L 	drop sequences with length shorter than INT
-M 	mask regions in BED or name list FILE
-N 	drop sequences containing ambiguous bases
-Q 	quality shift: ASCII-INT gives base quality
-R 	output both forward and reverse complement
-S 	strip of white spaces in sequences
-U 	convert all bases to uppercases
-V 	shift quality by '(-Q) - 33'
-X 	mask bases with quality higher than INT
-c 	mask complement region (effective with -M)
-f 	sample FLOAT fraction of sequences
-l 	number of residues per line; 0 for 2^32-1
-n 	masked bases converted to CHAR; 0 for lowercase
-q 	mask bases with quality lower than INT
-r 	reverse complement
-s 	random seed (effective with -f)
-x 	convert all lowercases to -n
--- seqtk seq -M data/
data/a.bam 
data/adapters.fasta 
data/notes.txt 
data/ont.fastq 
data/r1.fq.gz 
data/r2.fq.gz 
data/ref.fa 
data/regions.bed 
data/sub/
data/u.bam 
--- seqtk comp -r data/
data/regions.bed 
data/sub/
--- seqtk subseq data/ref.fa data/
data/a.bam 
data/adapters.fasta 
data/notes.txt 
data/ont.fastq 
data/r1.fq.gz 
data/r2.fq.gz 
data/ref.fa 
data/regions.bed 
data/sub/
data/u.bam 
--- seqtk mergepe data/r1.fq.gz data/
data/ont.fastq 
data/r1.fq.gz 
data/r2.fq.gz 
data/sub/
--- seqtk gc data/
data/adapters.fasta 
data/ref.fa 
data/sub/
--- seqtk mergepe -
